LOGBOOK.md-6-## 2026-08-30
LOGBOOK.md-7-
LOGBOOK.md-8-### Accepted M0 production bindings (TASK-260720-1qhxqa)
LOGBOOK.md-9-
LOGBOOK.md:10:- DECISION: Bound the exact reviewer-accepted generated-project, packet/HEV, and SSH outcome/verdict resource pairs plus the accepted M1 runtime contract in `Configuration/TASK-260720-1qhxqa_m0-production-bindings-v1.json`. Acceptance timestamps preserve upstream date precision instead of inventing a time of day.
LOGBOOK.md-11-- PERMIT: `productionCompositionPermitted=true` is only a recomputed result. `scripts/validate-m0-production-bindings.py` fails closed on digest drift, absence, malformed input, unknown schema/fields, stale/superseded evidence, a narrowed input set, negative/missing compatibility rows, and checked-in graph/native-pin drift.
LOGBOOK.md-12-- BINDINGS: macOS-only generated graph; MTU/buffers/batching/HEV values 1500/32768/64/5ms/24576/4096/2/500 with no HEV fork; selected pinned libssh2/OpenSSL adapter with exact algorithm, window, rekey, lifecycle, notice, maintenance, and revalidation constraints. Deferred iOS, MTU 4096/8500, whole-extension memory, general UDP, lanes, reconnect, and M3 tuning remain blocked/deferred.
LOGBOOK.md-13-- CONSUMER: `TASK-260715-3ejhyy` must use the machine manifest as its sole M0 binding source and validate it at the future macOS production factory entry point before concrete SSH/PacketFlowBridge/HEV construction or `NetworkSettingsApplier.apply`.
