LOGBOOK.md-970-### 2359 — Runtime model rework closes nested-version and fail-safe projection gaps (TASK-260715-lovbdz)
LOGBOOK.md-971-- REGRESSION: A schema-v1 `RuntimeStartRequest` previously accepted a nested `TunnelConfigurationReference` at schema 0 or 2 because only the outer header was checked. The nested decoder now returns the same stable `unsupportedSchemaVersion` error for both old and future versions.
LOGBOOK.md-972-- SAFETY: A future lifecycle `routeState` previously decoded as `unknown` while preserving true TCP, safe-DNS, route-installed, and health facts. Route state now participates in the shared fail-safe projection for both decoded and directly constructed lifecycle snapshots, forcing every capability false when it is unknown.
LOGBOOK.md-973-- COMPATIBILITY: Diagnostics generation and sequence remain required, while absent counters, gauges, histograms, and errors decode to their documented empty defaults. Explicit `null` or a wrong type remains corrupt rather than being treated as absence.
LOGBOOK.md-974-- VERIFICATION: Focused runtime codec tests and `make validate-core` pass; the full gate reports 183 tests in 21 suites plus boundary/native-package checks and a post-test build. Repository-wide Swift format lint, `git diff --check`, and `task-board validate` are clean.
LOGBOOK.md-975-
LOGBOOK.md-976-### 2344 — Runtime wire models make shared configuration secret-free by construction (TASK-260715-lovbdz)
LOGBOOK.md-977-- DECISION: M1 app messages use sorted-key protocol/schema v1 JSON with per-family 4/16/64 KiB limits and a strict bounded preflight that rejects invalid UTF-8, duplicate keys (including escape-equivalent keys), excessive nesting, corrupt numbers, trailing bytes, unsupported versions/kinds/values, and missing required fields before model use. The legacy `version` request/response remains the exact two-field v1 exception.
LOGBOOK.md-978-- SECURITY: The prior `TunnelConfiguration.parameters: [String:String]` escape hatch made private-key/passphrase exclusion structurally impossible. It was removed; provider/start configuration now contains only a schema-v1 UUID-backed profile reference, while configuration snapshots use distinct UUID-backed profile revision, credential, and trust references. Harness experiment parameters remain in harness-only recorded output and no longer cross into the runtime configuration.
LOGBOOK.md-979-- CAPABILITY: TCP, safe DNS, UDP, route mode, route-installed state, and health are independent required facts with no full-mode bit. Unknown output lifecycle/route values project to `unknown` with every capability false; generation/sequence ordering rejects lower generations and non-increasing snapshots.
LOGBOOK.md-980-- VERIFICATION: `make validate-core` passes boundary/native-package checks, 182 Swift tests in 21 suites, and a post-test build; repository-wide Swift format lint is clean. Tests cover every model round-trip, golden bytes, additive fields, old/future versions, hostile/corrupt/oversize input, secret-shape regression, redacted finite errors, legacy compatibility, and both platform roots.
LOGBOOK.md-981-
LOGBOOK.md:982:### 2317 — M1 runtime contract separates structural work from production M0 binding (TASK-260715-30zng6)
LOGBOOK.md-983-- DECISION: The packet-tunnel extension owns one actor-serialized runtime generation, with immutable app-message snapshots and no live forwarding dependency on the containing app. Startup is configuration -> verified/authenticated SSH -> TCP/DNS readiness -> pure packet preflight -> settings apply -> existing PacketBridge.start/read activation -> TCP + safe-DNS publication; every failure rolls back through one idempotent, non-cancellable stopping path.
LOGBOOK.md-984-- OWNERSHIP: M1PacketPlaneSession is the sole owner of the HEV private SOCKS boundary and dispatches authenticated CONNECT to TCP plus only approved virtual-DNS UDP/TCP to DNS; other UDP is rejected until M2. The coordinator proceeds against fakes independently of production factories, and both branches converge at TASK-260715-30ugfm.
LOGBOOK.md-985-- M0 GATE: TASK-260715-nphtib, TASK-260715-2jatnd, and TASK-260715-1gjxer currently have no reviewer-accepted outcome resources. New atomic TASK-260720-1qhxqa binds their future exact resources/digests and alone may set productionCompositionPermitted=true; TASK-260715-3ejhyy remains blocked behind it without delaying candidate-neutral models/coordinator work.
LOGBOOK.md-986-- SAFETY: Settings clear is called only after a committed or uncertain apply. A required failed/uncertain clear publishes capabilities false but truthfully retains routesInstalled=true with routeState=clearFailed; a clear that was unnecessary or confirmed publishes routesInstalled=false. Legacy version protocol v1 remains byte-exact while new M1 commands/snapshots use explicit schemas.
LOGBOOK.md-987-- REVIEW: Independent agent review requested and verified corrections across ownership, source-interface feasibility, versions, dependencies, transitions, and route cleanup, then accepted all five AC. PlantUML is unavailable and local Graphviz is broken by missing libltdl; authoritative sources and the toolchain anomaly are attached rather than claiming rendered evidence.
LOGBOOK.md-988-
LOGBOOK.md-989-### 2158 — Shared relay hostile corpus is semantically identical in Swift and Go (TASK-260715-297gq6)
LOGBOOK.md-990-- IMPLEMENTATION: Both protocol bindings consume the checked `lcg64-v1` regression corpus. Four fixed 64-bit seeds drive 2,096 deterministic cases across both envelope directions, legal and mutated frames, hostile declared lengths, arbitrary chunking/coalescing, inner HEV parsing, EOF, cancellation, and reset. Each language derives the same four stable semantic digests, so code/phase/scope/disposition or ordering drift fails the common gate without comparing implementation-specific error text.
LOGBOOK.md-991-- REVIEW REWORK: Decoder metrics now count internal byte/prefix/header/frame processing iterations and current/peak body-allocation bytes. Shared prefix-only cases declare exactly 4,096 bytes and 4,097 bytes, proving the accepted ceiling allocates at most 4,096 bytes and the next value allocates zero. The deterministic work ceiling is `inputBytes + 3 × bodyAllocations + 1`.
LOGBOOK.md-992-- BOUNDS: Swift and Go report the same 28,577 consumed bytes, 20-byte peak retained state, 4,096-byte peak allocated body, two maximum body allocations per case, 42 maximum processing iterations against a 43-iteration maximum ceiling, five maximum chunks, 96-byte diagnostics, and zero retained/outstanding body bytes after every terminal and reset path. Successful output records each exact seed ID, value, and semantic digest without payload content.
LOGBOOK.md-993-- VERIFICATION: `make relay-protocol-check`, Go checkptr, Swift AddressSanitizer, strict Swift format, gofmt, Go vet, shell syntax, JSON validation, diff validation, and board validation pass. A five-second native Go fuzz run passed 1,453,381 executions with 19 new coverage-interesting inputs and no crash/invariant failure. Protocol source coverage is Swift 93.21% (1,797/1,928 lines) and Go 85.7% statements.
LOGBOOK.md-994-- TOOLCHAIN: The repository still lacks the authoritative `relay/go.mod` and pinned Go 1.26.5 owned by TASK-260715-27uz4n, so local Go evidence uses the accepted standard-library-only `CGO_ENABLED=0` smoke under Go 1.25.5. This does not substitute for the later release-toolchain gate.
